nt who raised the turn.\n\n4. **All-in (-2)**: Maximum aggression with 17,732 chips. Too risky with just one pair against an opponent showing strength.\n\n**Reason:**\nThe opponent's turn raise is concerning, but I have pot odds to call and see the river. My pair of Jacks with Ace kicker could still be good, or I could improve to two pair or trips on the river. Re-raising or going all-in with just one pair against a turn raise is too risky. Folding wastes the investment I've made. Calling preserves chips while keeping me alive in the hand.\n\n**Answer:** 0"}
